{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794606631892,"sessionID":"ses_e292e55ddffeFGrUddLBqtwaO3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-deeb3383-928c-479d-bc98-c55c311428bd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/record/record.py","oldString":"if name == \"check-anchors\":\n            p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None,\n                           help=\"esplora API base; default blockstream.info and mempool.space\")","newString":"if name == \"check-anchors\":\n            p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None,\n                           help=\"esplora API base; default blockstream.info and mempool.space\")\n            p.add_argument(\"--max-pending-hours\", type=int, metavar=\"H\",\n                           help=\"fail if a range head's OTS proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation is over H hours old\")"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -611,8 +611,10 @@\n if name == \"check-anchors\":\n     p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n     p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None,\n                    help=\"esplora API base; default blockstream.info and mempool.space\")\n+    p.add_argument(\"--max-pending-hours\", type=int, metavar=\"H\",\n+                   help=\"fail if a range head's OTS proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation is over H hours old\")\n else:\n     p.add_argument(\"--only-ref\", help=\"check this ref only (default: every ref GitHub names)\")\n     p.add_argument(\"--ledger-ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\", help=\"the ledger's branch; a force push to it is wrong\")\n     p.add_argument(\"--git-rev\", default=\"HEAD\", help=\"the ledger branch's history in this clone (for orphan checks)\")\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/record/record.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -611,8 +611,10 @@\n if name == \"check-anchors\":\n     p.add_argument(\"--ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\")\n     p.add_argument(\"--explorer\", action=\"append\", default=None,\n                    help=\"esplora API base; default blockstream.info and mempool.space\")\n+    p.add_argument(\"--max-pending-hours\", type=int, metavar=\"H\",\n+                   help=\"fail if a range head's OTS proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation is over H hours old\")\n else:\n     p.add_argument(\"--only-ref\", help=\"check this ref only (default: every ref GitHub names)\")\n     p.add_argument(\"--ledger-ref\", default=\"refs/heads/main\", help=\"the ledger's branch; a force push to it is wrong\")\n     p.add_argument(\"--git-rev\", default=\"HEAD\", help=\"the ledger branch's history in this clone (for orphan checks)\")\n","additions":2,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/record/record.py","time":{"start":1794606631881,"end":1794606631891}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good, all tests pass. Now I need to implement the `--max-pending-hours` option for `check-anchors`. Let me analyze the code more carefully:\n\n1. In `cmd_check_anchors`, the function processes anchors and checks OTS proofs\n2. `check_ots` returns the earliest Bitcoin block time or `None` if still pending\n3. The Sigstore attestation time is returned by `check_sigstore` as `t` (integrated_time)\n4. I need to track for each range head (the `hi` in ranges) what its Sigstore attestation time is\n5. When an OTS proof is pending (returns `None`), check if the attestation time is more than H hours ago\n\nLooking at the code flow:\n- `ranges` contains tuples of `(from_seq, to_seq, commit)` for each Sigstore anchor\n- `stamped` contains the sequence numbers that have `.ots` files\n- For each range head `hi`, if `hi not in stamped`, it's an error\n- But if `hi in stamped` and the OTS proof is pending, we need to check the age\n\nThe key insight is that we need to associate each range head with its Sigstore attestation time. The Sigstore anchor for sequence `hi` gives us the attestation time `t`.\n\nLet me modify the code to:\n1. Add `--max-pending-hours` argument to the check-anchors parser\n2. Track the attestation time for each range head\n3. When checking OTS proofs, if pending and max_pending_hours is set, check if attestation time is older than H hours\n4. Print error message with \"still pending N h\" format\n\nLet me implement this.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d6e40bc3001SXCnPmmPLDtoMt","sessionID":"ses_e292e55ddffeFGrUddLBqtwaO3","messageID":"msg_1d6e0492f001hH3ZffoBs9JPlO"}}
