{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794607476695,"sessionID":"ses_e292e55ddffeFGrUddLBqtwaO3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-37024e04-2aed-4009-a42e-859d4a505d96","state":{"status":"error","input":{"command":"cd /tmp && rm -rf test_ledger && mkdir -p test_ledger/entries test_ledger/anchors test_ledger/inbox && cd /workspace/record && python3 record.py --ledger /tmp/test_ledger ingest << 'EOF'\n{\"kind\": \"plan\", \"body\": {\"by\": \"tester\", \"claim\": \"test\", \"test\": \"test\", \"decision_rule\": \"test\"}}\nEOF"},"error":"The user rejected permission to use this specific tool call.","time":{"start":1794607476677,"end":1794607476686}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The help shows the new option. Now let me create a quick test to verify the functionality works as expected. I'll need to create a test ledger with a pending OTS proof and an old attestation time. But since the tests use stubs for `check_ots` and `check_sigstore`, let me write a quick integration test to verify the logic.\n\nActually, let me look at the existing test `test_a_missing_ots_proof_for_a_range_head_is_caught` more carefully - it stubs both `check_sigstore` and `check_ots`. The stub for `check_sigstore` returns `(1, predicate, \"c0ffee\")` where `1` is the attestation time (integrated_time). The stub for `check_ots` returns `None` (pending).\n\nWith my implementation, when `check_ots` returns `None`, it checks if `seq in attestation_times` and if `hours_pending > max_pending_hours`. Since the stub returns attestation time `1` (which is 1970-01-01), and current time is 2026, the hours_pending would be huge.\n\nBut wait - the test doesn't use `--max-pending-hours`, so it should still pass (which it does). Let me verify the logic by running with `--max-pending-hours 1` on the test's stub scenario.\n\nActually, the test creates a stub `.sigstore.json` file and stubs `check_sigstore` to return `(1, ...)`. The attestation time `1` is the Unix timestamp 1 (1970-01-01 00:00:01 UTC). With `--max-pending-hours 1`, this would be way over the limit.\n\nBut the test doesn't pass `--max-pending-hours`, so `a.max_pending_hours` is `None`, and the check is skipped. That's correct.\n\nLet me write a quick manual test to verify the feature works.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d6f0efc1001dQDmTWp6Xaue5V","sessionID":"ses_e292e55ddffeFGrUddLBqtwaO3","messageID":"msg_1d6ec6eb0001gnOK4Lr2DTuVfy"}}
